    "title": "The Life of a Star",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PM9CQDlQI0A",
    "spec": "Build an interactive web app that explores the evolution of stars based on their initial mass. \n\nSPECIFICATIONS:\n1. Provide a slider to select the initial mass of the star (from 0.1 to 100 solar masses).\n2. Display a timeline or 'Advance' button to move through the star's life stages.\n3. Show a visual representation of the star (size, color, and features like nebulas, supergiants, pulsars, or black holes).\n4. Provide textual descriptions of the physical processes at each stage (e.g., fusion, collapse, supernova).\n5. Include an 'H-R Diagram' visualization that shows the star's current position as it evolves.",
    "code": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Stellar Evolution Interactive</title>\n    <style>\n        :root {\n            --bg-color: #050510;\n            --text-color: #e0e0f0;\n            --accent-color: #4a9eff;\n        }\n        body {\n            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;\n            background-color: var(--bg-color);\n            color: var(--text-color);\n            margin: 0;\n            padding: 20px;\n            display: flex;\n            flex-direction: column;\n            align-items: center;\n            min-height: 100vh;\n        }\n        .container {\n            max-width: 900px;\n            width: 100%;\n            display: grid;\n            grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n            gap: 20px;\n        }\n        @media (max-width: 768px) {\n            .container { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n        }\n        .visual-panel {\n            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);\n            border-radius: 12px;\n            padding: 20px;\n            display: flex;\n            flex-direction: column;\n            align-items: center;\n            justify-content: center;\n            position: relative;\n            min-height: 400px;\n            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);\n        }\n        .info-panel {\n            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);\n            border-radius: 12px;\n            padding: 20px;\n            display: flex;\n            flex-direction: column;\n            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);\n        }\n        .star-container {\n            width: 300px;\n            height: 300px;\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            justify-content: center;\n            position: relative;\n        }\n        .star {\n            border-radius: 50%;\n            transition: all 1s ease-in-out;\n            box-shadow: 0 0 40px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n            position: relative;\n        }\n        .nebula {\n            position: absolute;\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 100%;\n            background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(160, 50, 200, 0.4) 0%, transparent 70%);\n            border-radius: 50%;\n            filter: blur(20px);\n            opacity: 1;\n            transition: opacity 1s;\n        }\n        .controls {\n            grid-column: 1 / -1;\n            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);\n            padding: 20px;\n            border-radius: 12px;\n            display: flex;\n            flex-direction: column;\n            gap: 15px;\n        }\n        .slider-group {\n            display: flex;\n            flex-direction: column;\n            gap: 8px;\n        }\n        input[type=range] {\n            width: 100%;\n            cursor: pointer;\n        }\n        .stats {\n            display: flex;\n            justify-content: space-between;\n            font-size: 0.9em;\n            color: #aaa;\n        }\n        .stage-title {\n            font-size: 1.5em;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            color: var(--accent-color);\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\n        }\n        .description {\n            line-height: 1.6;\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\n        }\n        button {\n            background: var(--accent-color);\n            color: white;\n            border: none;\n            padding: 10px 20px;\n            border-radius: 6px;\n            cursor: pointer;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            transition: background 0.2s;\n        }\n        button:hover {\n            filter: brightness(1.1);\n        }\n        button:disabled {\n            background: #444;\n            cursor: not-allowed;\n        }\n        .hr-diagram {\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 200px;\n            background: #111;\n            margin-top: auto;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            position: relative;\n            padding: 5px;\n            box-sizing: border-box;\n            border: 1px solid #333;\n        }\n        .hr-label {\n            position: absolute;\n            font-size: 10px;\n            color: #666;\n        }\n        .hr-point {\n            width: 6px;\n            height: 6px;\n            background: var(--accent-color);\n            border-radius: 50%;\n            position: absolute;\n            transition: all 0.5s;\n            box-shadow: 0 0 5px currentColor;\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <h1>The Life of a Star</h1>\n    \n    <div class=\"container\">\n        <div class=\"controls\">\n            <div class=\"slider-group\">\n                <label>Initial Stellar Mass: <span id=\"mass-value\">1.0</span> M☉</label>\n                <input type=\"range\" id=\"mass-slider\" min=\"0.1\" max=\"50\" step=\"0.1\" value=\"1.0\">\n                <div class=\"stats\">\n                    <span>Low Mass (0.1M☉)</span>\n                    <span>High Mass (50M☉)</span>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: center;\">\n                <button id=\"advance-btn\">Advance Stage</button>\n                <button id=\"reset-btn\">Reset Star</button>\n                <div id=\"age-display\" style=\"margin-left: auto; color: #888;\">Age: 0 million years</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"visual-panel\">\n            <div class=\"star-container\">\n                <div id=\"nebula\" class=\"nebula\"></div>\n                <div id=\"star\" class=\"star\" style=\"width: 50px; height: 50px; background: #fff;\"></div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"info-panel\">\n            <div id=\"stage-name\" class=\"stage-title\">Protostar</div>\n            <div id=\"stage-desc\" class=\"description\">A cloud of gas and dust is collapsing under gravity. Temperature and density are rising in the core.</div>\n            \n            <div class=\"hr-diagram\">\n                <div class=\"hr-label\" style=\"bottom: 5px; right: 5px;\">Temp (K)</div>\n                <div class=\"hr-label\" style=\"top: 5px; left: 5px;\">Lum (L☉)</div>\n                <div id=\"hr-point\" class=\"hr-point\" style=\"bottom: 20%; left: 80%;\"></div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <script>\n        const massSlider = document.getElementById('mass-slider');\n        const massValue = document.getElementById('mass-value');\n        const advanceBtn = document.getElementById('advance-btn');\n        const resetBtn = document.getElementById('reset-btn');\n        const star = document.getElementById('star');\n        const nebula = document.getElementById('nebula');\n        const stageName = document.getElementById('stage-name');\n        const stageDesc = document.getElementById('stage-desc');\n        const ageDisplay = document.getElementById('age-display');\n        const hrPoint = document.getElementById('hr-point');\n\n        let currentStage = 0;\n        let mass = 1.0;\n\n        const getEvolution = (m) => {\n            if (m < 0.8) {\n                return [\n                    { name: 'Protostar', desc: 'Gravitational collapse of molecular cloud.', size: 40, color: 'rgba(255,150,0,0.5)', hr: [20, 80], age: 0 },\n                    { name: 'Main Sequence (Red Dwarf)', desc: 'Hydrogen fusion at a slow, steady rate. These stars live for trillions of years.', size: 30, color: '#ff4d00', hr: [10, 90], age: 100 },\n                    { name: 'Red Dwarf', desc: 'Slowly burning through its fuel. Most of its life is spent here.', size: 28, color: '#ff4d00', hr: [8, 92], age: 10000 },\n                    { name: 'White Dwarf', desc: 'After eons, it runs out of hydrogen and slowly cools down.', size: 10, color: '#aaccff', hr: [80, 20], age: 1000000 }\n                ];\n            } else if (m < 8) {\n                return [\n                    { name: 'Protostar', desc: 'Forming from a stellar nursery.', size: 60, color: 'rgba(255,200,100,0.6)', hr: [40, 80], age: 0 },\n                    { name: 'Main Sequence (Sun-like)', desc: 'Fusing hydrogen into helium. Stable equilibrium between gravity and radiation pressure.', size: 50, color: '#fffb00', hr: [50, 50], age: 500 },\n                    { name: 'Red Giant', desc: 'Hydrogen exhausted. The star expands as helium fusion begins in the core.', size: 150, color: '#ff4400', hr: [30, 10], age: 10000 },\n                    { name: 'Planetary Nebula', desc: 'Outer layers are ejected into space, exposing the dense core.', size: 200, color: 'rgba(0,255,255,0.2)', hr: [60, 30], age: 10500, isNebula: true },\n                    { name: 'White Dwarf', desc: 'The hot, dense core remains. No further fusion occurs.', size: 12, color: '#ffffff', hr: [85, 40], age: 11000 }\n                ];\n            } else {\n                return [\n                    { name: 'Protostar', desc: 'Rapid formation from massive gas clouds.', size: 100, color: 'rgba(100,200,255,0.7)', hr: [60, 60], age: 0 },\n                    { name: 'Blue Supergiant', desc: 'Incredibly hot and luminous. Burning fuel at an unsustainable rate.', size: 80, color: '#00ccff', hr: [90, 10], age: 10 },\n                    { name: 'Red Supergiant', desc: 'Fusing heavier elements (Carbon, Neon, Iron). The largest stars in the universe.', size: 220, color: '#ff2200', hr: [20, 5], age: 15 },\n                    { name: 'Supernova', desc: 'Core collapse creates a massive explosion, spreading elements across the galaxy.', size: 300, color: '#ffffff', hr: [95, 5], age: 16, isExplosion: true },\n                    { name: 'Neutron Star / Black Hole', desc: 'A tiny, extremely dense remnant remains. Intense gravity bends light.', size: 5, color: '#000', hr: [5, 95], age: 20 }\n                ];\n            }\n        };\n\n        const updateStar = () => {\n            const stages = getEvolution(mass);\n            if (currentStage >= stages.length) currentStage = stages.length - 1;\n            \n            const s = stages[currentStage];\n            stageName.textContent = s.name;\n            stageDesc.textContent = s.desc;\n            ageDisplay.textContent = `Age: ${s.age} million years`;\n            \n            star.style.width = s.size + 'px';\n            star.style.height = s.size + 'px';\n            star.style.background = s.isExplosion ? 'radial-gradient(circle, #fff, #ff0, transparent)' : s.color;\n            star.style.boxShadow = s.isExplosion ? '0 0 100px #fff' : `0 0 40px ${s.color}`;\n            star.style.opacity = s.name === 'Black Hole' ? '0.2' : '1';\n            \n            nebula.style.opacity = s.isNebula ? '1' : '0';\n            \n            hrPoint.style.left = s.hr[0] + '%';\n            hrPoint.style.bottom = s.hr[1] + '%';\n            hrPoint.style.color = s.color;\n\n            advanceBtn.disabled = currentStage === stages.length - 1;\n        };\n\n        massSlider.oninput = (e) => {\n            mass = parseFloat(e.target.value);\n            massValue.textContent = mass.toFixed(1);\n            currentStage = 0;\n            updateStar();\n        };\n\n        advanceBtn.onclick = () => {\n            currentStage++;\n            updateStar();\n        };\n\n        resetBtn.onclick = () => {\n            currentStage = 0;\n            updateStar();\n        };\n\n        updateStar();\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>"
  }
]
